"Ada Pell will vouch for someone to a magistrate once they have worked her kitchen a fortnight."
"Brannock files a no-card stranger as a 'lost person' if she is calm, and as a suspect if she lies."
"Brannock's cell has held three suspected Sedhahns this winter; all turned out to be drunk locals."
"Wren would pay a reader five crowns a day, cash, to read him sequence manuals and fine glyphs."
"Wren knows in his bones that an arcanist can teach an untaught adult, whatever the schools say."
"Mirelle Osk fences restricted artefacts for the barge smugglers and pays in cash."
"Osk would pay forty crowns for clothes of a weave and cut no one in Aiesta has seen."
"The Lantern Rooms' keeper, Jory Tate, tips off Osk about any guest worth robbing."
"A gang called the Weir Rats, boys and girls of fourteen to twenty, rob drunks after dark."
